comments.body:
@participant1

- `192.168.1.11` is the machine DHCP IP Address
- `192.168.201.90` is the router Internet IP Address

@participant1 @participant3 Tagging you as you worked/reviewed and seem knowledgable about this upnp stuff: Is there an actual indication of broken functionality here?

I have very little knowledge of this and looking at the logs it's not entirely clear, as error messages are mixed with informational messages of successful upnp operations. From a cursory glance it's not clear to me if things are working as intended and we are just too verbose with accompanying failed attempts, or if there's actual degraded functionality that could/should be improved/fixed.

Regardless of which of the two it is, it looks like there's potential to reduce the verboseness. We don't need to spam the log with the same error over and over (just different port, I assume those are retries). A single message surely would suffice (if attempted ports are important info, those can be added to that single log entry).
